1
00:00:50,680 --> 00:00:53,060
Thank you.

2
00:01:29,880 --> 00:01:33,000
I was totally psyched to go
on a class trip to Kyoto,

3
00:01:33,300 --> 00:01:35,537
but my trip was rudely
interrupted by Blackboard

4
00:01:35,620 --> 00:01:37,737
Raymon destroying another Destiny Stone.

5
00:01:37,820 --> 00:01:40,597
I followed him and some
other strange Digimon, too.

6
00:01:40,680 --> 00:01:43,477
Shurimon and Stingmon were able to
send them back to the digital world,

7
00:01:43,560 --> 00:01:46,657
but I had to do a lot of explaining
to Joe's brother and Sora's father.

8
00:01:46,740 --> 00:01:48,757
they had their own
theory about how magical

9
00:01:48,840 --> 00:01:50,857
creatures have been known to visit Kyoto.

10
00:01:50,940 --> 00:01:53,040
Right, if they only knew the truth.

11
00:01:53,420 --> 00:01:56,717
Meanwhile, Arukinima told us she
has plans for a trip of her own,

12
00:01:56,800 --> 00:01:59,637
to find the other five destiny
stones and destroy them.

13
00:01:59,720 --> 00:02:02,426
That would totally
demolish the digital world.

14
00:02:06,240 --> 00:02:07,760
Holy point, mamore!

15
00:02:09,940 --> 00:02:12,528
There must be some kind
of answer out there.

16
00:02:12,680 --> 00:02:14,760
Who I am, what I'm meant to do.

17
00:02:15,320 --> 00:02:19,320
Alas, until I find it, I must follow
the call of the Destiny Stones.

18
00:02:20,640 --> 00:02:22,777
This is a pleasant drive, don't you think?

19
00:02:22,860 --> 00:02:25,537
Well, it would be if someone didn't
keep interrupting my thoughts.

20
00:02:25,620 --> 00:02:27,797
Sorry, I'll look at him
up, but I'm close to you.

21
00:02:27,880 --> 00:02:28,710
I just...

22
00:02:29,240 --> 00:02:30,070
Just...

23
00:02:30,153 --> 00:02:31,660
Just concentrate on the driving.

24
00:02:36,100 --> 00:02:36,930
Yum!

25
00:02:37,160 --> 00:02:38,600
I'll say. Mmm!

26
00:02:38,860 --> 00:02:40,277
Snacks, your meat bread are sure.

27
00:02:40,360 --> 00:02:41,337
It's good and delicious.

28
00:02:41,420 --> 00:02:43,200
I can eat them all day. Hey!

29
00:02:45,100 --> 00:02:46,240
That's not fair.

30
00:02:46,440 --> 00:02:48,040
Save one for me. Just one!

31
00:02:48,260 --> 00:02:50,877
I never thought I'd see
Black War Greymon in Kyoto.

32
00:02:50,960 --> 00:02:52,457
That wasn't in the travel brochure.

33
00:02:52,540 --> 00:02:54,837
I don't understand why he showed up there.

34
00:02:54,920 --> 00:02:55,750
Well,

35
00:02:55,833 --> 00:02:58,197
Sora's father said that Kyoto's
at a kind of crossroads where

36
00:02:58,280 --> 00:03:01,797
the spiritual world and our world
sometimes cross over each other.

37
00:03:01,880 --> 00:03:04,177
That's why they built all
those temples there to

38
00:03:04,260 --> 00:03:06,857
protect this world from
otherworldly creatures.

39
00:03:06,940 --> 00:03:09,357
And they say that every
Halloween night you can see

40
00:03:09,440 --> 00:03:12,675
twisted ghostly figures
wandering the streets of Kyoto.

41
00:03:12,800 --> 00:03:14,506
Those stories don't scare me.

42
00:03:14,760 --> 00:03:18,677
Though they wouldn't be something to
consider if they're true, are they?

43
00:03:18,760 --> 00:03:22,717
But if a Digimon appeared in the real
world, that's not just a child's story.

44
00:03:22,800 --> 00:03:25,717
That means the digital world's
plane is really off-kilter.

45
00:03:25,800 --> 00:03:26,630
Yeah.

46
00:03:26,713 --> 00:03:31,157
But wait, if the digital world's plane is
off-kilter, why is it affecting our world?

47
00:03:31,240 --> 00:03:32,340
It's like this.

48
00:03:32,720 --> 00:03:37,308
Imagine this is the digital world, and
this line is our world, the real world.

49
00:03:37,860 --> 00:03:39,617
Normally, they're kept separately.

50
00:03:39,700 --> 00:03:41,660
But if the plane gets off-kilter,

51
00:03:41,820 --> 00:03:45,055
they start mixing together,
and then nothing is normal.

52
00:03:45,540 --> 00:03:47,400
Thanks, even I understand now.

53
00:03:47,700 --> 00:03:48,641
Thank God, Oman.

54
00:03:48,800 --> 00:03:50,280
She explained it. Mm-hmm.

55
00:03:51,020 --> 00:03:53,491
And that dark ocean is another world, too.

56
00:03:55,540 --> 00:03:57,040
That's not all. Huh?

57
00:03:57,240 --> 00:04:00,837
I'd be willing to bet that there's a whole
bunch of other worlds out there as well.

58
00:04:00,920 --> 00:04:01,760
Like this.

59
00:04:03,800 --> 00:04:04,800
Like a rainbow.

60
00:04:05,140 --> 00:04:07,717
But look what happens if
the balance is destroyed.

61
00:04:07,800 --> 00:04:10,212
Looks like it's all going down the drain.

62
00:04:12,200 --> 00:04:13,030
Whack.

63
00:04:13,580 --> 00:04:14,680
And in the end,

64
00:04:14,840 --> 00:04:17,637
every world might be covered
in darkness As dark as a

65
00:04:17,720 --> 00:04:21,480
black cat at midnight We can't
let that happen You're right,

66
00:04:21,600 --> 00:04:25,718
and that's exactly why we have to
protect the remaining Destiny Stones

67
00:04:25,900 --> 00:04:32,700
Hi Hey, Izzy, great timing Just hold on I
got you a decorative dish towel Cute, huh?

68
00:04:33,020 --> 00:04:37,337
Yeah, thanks, Yoli, and I have a gift for
you guys, too You hate the towel, right?

69
00:04:37,420 --> 00:04:40,460
I've written an algorithm
for the D3 and D-Terminal

70
00:04:40,940 --> 00:04:42,280
Once I transferred in,

71
00:04:42,420 --> 00:04:45,537
we'll be able to use the D-terminal
to see the rift in the plane.

72
00:04:45,620 --> 00:04:46,480
There we go.

73
00:04:47,140 --> 00:04:48,611
Wow, Izzy, this is great.

74
00:04:48,840 --> 00:04:51,437
We can use this to track
down Black War Greymon.

75
00:04:51,520 --> 00:04:55,337
Well, gee, it's the least I can do
after Yoli got me that neat towel.

76
00:04:55,420 --> 00:04:57,200
So you do like the towel, yay!

77
00:04:57,500 --> 00:04:59,700
Let's go mop up Black War Greymon!

78
00:05:00,160 --> 00:05:01,336
Wait, I've got mail.

79
00:05:02,060 --> 00:05:05,766
Geez, Kari, you'd think that I've
got mail is your middle name.

80
00:05:06,020 --> 00:05:07,800
Yeah, Kari, check that later.

81
00:05:08,680 --> 00:05:09,840
Digi-port open!

82
00:05:10,140 --> 00:05:12,669
Let's go save the
Digi-world one more time!

83
00:05:19,040 --> 00:05:20,517
Where's Black War Greymon?

84
00:05:20,600 --> 00:05:22,177
I want to teach him a lesson or two.

85
00:05:22,260 --> 00:05:23,460
Like three or four.

86
00:05:23,880 --> 00:05:25,040
He's over that way.

87
00:05:25,180 --> 00:05:26,217
All right, then let's go.

88
00:05:26,300 --> 00:05:29,040
Aw, I got sand between
my toes. And your ears.

89
00:05:29,640 --> 00:05:32,980
The Destiny Stone almost looks
too beautiful to destroy.

90
00:05:33,400 --> 00:05:34,460
But I must.

91
00:05:34,740 --> 00:05:37,297
Boy, I sure wish I could
fly and so do my poor feet!

92
00:05:37,380 --> 00:05:39,040
We're getting really close.

93
00:05:39,240 --> 00:05:40,340
It's about time.

94
00:05:40,520 --> 00:05:41,440
Hey, it's Ken.

95
00:05:41,740 --> 00:05:42,880
Davis, hurry up.

96
00:05:43,040 --> 00:05:44,020
I'm trying to.

97
00:05:44,420 --> 00:05:45,600
Well, hurry faster.

98
00:05:45,920 --> 00:05:46,750
Don't wait for me.

99
00:05:46,833 --> 00:05:47,900
Go on ahead. Okay.

100
00:05:51,440 --> 00:05:52,640
Terra Destroyer.

101
00:05:55,400 --> 00:05:56,840
My, my, my.

102
00:05:57,200 --> 00:05:58,200
Such power.

103
00:05:58,700 --> 00:06:00,400
Yeah, but he only nicked it.

104
00:06:02,660 --> 00:06:03,860
Terra Destroyer.

105
00:06:05,140 --> 00:06:07,140
Oh, that's a solid shot.

106
00:06:09,580 --> 00:06:11,600
Now only four stones remain.

107
00:06:15,420 --> 00:06:16,460
What? Huh?

108
00:06:17,020 --> 00:06:18,280
Could this be it?

109
00:06:18,440 --> 00:06:20,322
The foe I've been searching for?

110
00:06:20,520 --> 00:06:24,344
Perhaps I'm drawing even closer
by destroying the Destiny Stones.

111
00:06:24,600 --> 00:06:25,640
Do you see that?

112
00:06:25,800 --> 00:06:26,837
Gee, I'm not sure.

113
00:06:26,920 --> 00:06:28,377
It's only a hundred feet tall.

114
00:06:28,460 --> 00:06:30,800
But whatever it was, it's gone now.

115
00:06:31,900 --> 00:06:32,730
No.

116
00:06:32,813 --> 00:06:33,680
No, this can't be.

117
00:06:34,040 --> 00:06:37,334
After all my searching, my
opponent can't just run away.

118
00:06:38,380 --> 00:06:39,210
No!

119
00:06:39,840 --> 00:06:43,540
I must destroy another
stone to draw out my foe.

120
00:06:43,860 --> 00:06:45,280
He is not happy.

121
00:06:45,980 --> 00:06:47,420
Yes, but I am.

122
00:06:48,620 --> 00:06:51,657
But what if that creature in
the Destiny Stone gets loose

123
00:06:51,740 --> 00:06:54,577
and then gets mad at us for
creating Blackborn Greymon?

124
00:06:54,660 --> 00:06:55,540
Big deal.

125
00:06:55,940 --> 00:06:56,820
You sure?

126
00:06:57,420 --> 00:06:58,837
Yes, you sniveling coward.

127
00:06:58,920 --> 00:06:59,802
Now step on it.

128
00:07:00,540 --> 00:07:01,640
Slow down.

129
00:07:02,720 --> 00:07:03,660
Oh, no.

130
00:07:05,540 --> 00:07:07,260
We got here too late.

131
00:07:07,480 --> 00:07:09,900
Another stone destroyed. What'll we do?

132
00:07:10,020 --> 00:07:13,397
At this rate, they'll all be destroyed
before we can stop Blackboard Greymon.

133
00:07:13,480 --> 00:07:14,310
No.

134
00:07:15,000 --> 00:07:17,797
There's no way I'm going to
stand by and let some soulless

135
00:07:17,880 --> 00:07:21,057
creature made from evil control
spires destroy the digital world.

136
00:07:21,140 --> 00:07:23,120
I want that ugly thing destroyed.

137
00:07:23,520 --> 00:07:25,260
I've never seen TK so angry.

138
00:07:25,800 --> 00:07:27,240
No, that's not true.

139
00:07:27,540 --> 00:07:28,560
In the tunnels.

140
00:07:31,920 --> 00:07:34,332
Oh, it's like there are two sides to him.

141
00:07:34,600 --> 00:07:35,940
Two people inside him.

142
00:07:36,160 --> 00:07:39,717
Okay, we'll have all the Digimon in the
area locate the other Destiny Stones.

143
00:07:39,800 --> 00:07:42,976
That should give us the edge
of her Black War Greymon.

144
00:07:43,260 --> 00:07:44,960
So who is talking now?

145
00:07:45,200 --> 00:07:47,760
The rational TK or the angry one?

146
00:07:48,100 --> 00:07:49,960
And which one is the real TK?

147
00:07:50,500 --> 00:07:53,577
It galls me to have been
so close to the opponent I

148
00:07:53,660 --> 00:07:56,537
so hungrily seek only to
have him ripped away from me.

149
00:07:56,620 --> 00:07:58,200
I must find him.

150
00:08:01,400 --> 00:08:02,840
See you tomorrow, guys.

151
00:08:04,000 --> 00:08:04,917
Hasta la...

152
00:08:05,000 --> 00:08:07,160
Um, boink, but... Uh, see ya!

153
00:08:08,900 --> 00:08:09,730
Huh?

154
00:08:10,020 --> 00:08:12,057
Cody, don't you have kendo practice?

155
00:08:12,140 --> 00:08:12,970
What's that?

156
00:08:13,120 --> 00:08:14,780
Oh, yes, I do. Thank you.

157
00:08:17,040 --> 00:08:17,870
Hmm.

158
00:08:19,400 --> 00:08:20,817
What's up with you, Cody?

159
00:08:20,900 --> 00:08:21,760
You seem sad.

160
00:08:24,000 --> 00:08:25,640
Is it Black War Greymon?

161
00:08:26,900 --> 00:08:28,477
No, Bumon. It's...

162
00:08:28,560 --> 00:08:29,480
TK.

163
00:08:30,140 --> 00:08:34,081
I'm worried that he and I will have
to DNA Digivolve together soon.

164
00:08:35,080 --> 00:08:37,457
But there'd be nothing
better, would there?

165
00:08:37,540 --> 00:08:38,420
I don't know.

166
00:08:38,680 --> 00:08:41,777
I thought I knew who TK
was, but now it's like he...

167
00:08:41,860 --> 00:08:45,617
Sometimes it just seems like he's
a completely different person.

168
00:08:45,700 --> 00:08:47,517
Maybe you're just getting
to know him better.

169
00:08:47,600 --> 00:08:50,917
Just because you see a new side to
someone, it doesn't mean it's a bad side.

170
00:08:51,000 --> 00:08:52,077
Look at us, Digimon.

171
00:08:52,160 --> 00:08:53,157
We change all the time,

172
00:08:53,240 --> 00:08:56,697
I don't hear you complaining about
us getting you out of Tufts' graves.

173
00:08:56,780 --> 00:08:58,956
Unless you do it when I'm not around.

174
00:08:59,220 --> 00:09:01,808
You don't do it when
I'm not around, do you?

175
00:09:04,300 --> 00:09:05,260
No. No!

176
00:09:05,780 --> 00:09:08,577
I've got to stop Black War
Greymon before he destroys

177
00:09:08,660 --> 00:09:11,719
the digital world and all
the Digimon along with it.

178
00:09:12,220 --> 00:09:14,020
Digimon! Digimon, no!

179
00:09:21,940 --> 00:09:23,000
You're safe.

180
00:09:26,100 --> 00:09:30,740
Soon we shall meet my nemesis, and I
will find a purpose for my existence.

181
00:09:31,440 --> 00:09:32,920
It's scary up here.

182
00:09:33,260 --> 00:09:34,637
There's nothing to be afraid of.

183
00:09:34,720 --> 00:09:35,777
Just don't look down.

184
00:09:35,860 --> 00:09:36,980
I look down.

185
00:09:37,200 --> 00:09:39,040
Now I can't stop looking down.

186
00:09:41,500 --> 00:09:43,120
Just a few more steps.

187
00:09:44,520 --> 00:09:45,800
Come on, Kari!

188
00:09:48,800 --> 00:09:49,630
Kari!

189
00:09:51,620 --> 00:09:54,960
Are you okay now, Kari? Yeah. Okay.

190
00:09:56,260 --> 00:09:57,580
I'm too slow!

191
00:09:58,140 --> 00:10:01,277
Did the Digimon find where
the other Destiny Stones are?

192
00:10:01,360 --> 00:10:03,000
I'd bet my nine lives.

193
00:10:03,200 --> 00:10:04,280
Yeah, undoubtedly.

194
00:10:09,040 --> 00:10:11,500
Looks like it's me and you, Cody. Yep.

195
00:10:12,040 --> 00:10:13,460
Hey, don't overlook me!

196
00:10:14,020 --> 00:10:15,080
Ah, Gabumon!

197
00:10:15,880 --> 00:10:16,710
Hi, guys.

198
00:10:16,960 --> 00:10:19,877
There's a destiny stone
just over these mountains.

199
00:10:19,960 --> 00:10:20,897
Thanks, Gabumon.

200
00:10:20,980 --> 00:10:22,877
Well, a little hike never hurt anyone.

201
00:10:22,960 --> 00:10:25,217
Yeah, unless, of course,
your boots are too small.

202
00:10:25,300 --> 00:10:27,397
Listen, there's something
else I need to tell you.

203
00:10:27,480 --> 00:10:28,817
It seems that...

204
00:10:28,900 --> 00:10:30,371
You can tell us, Gabumon.

205
00:10:30,720 --> 00:10:33,180
Black War Greymon has a heart. He what?

206
00:10:34,220 --> 00:10:36,997
I know it may be hard to
believe, but it's true.

207
00:10:37,080 --> 00:10:37,910
But how?

208
00:10:37,993 --> 00:10:40,597
I mean, he's only made
from control spires, right?

209
00:10:40,680 --> 00:10:43,060
I know, I know, but Agumon told me so.

210
00:10:43,580 --> 00:10:47,297
No creature without a heart could ask
the soul-searching questions he asks.

211
00:10:47,380 --> 00:10:52,321
But then, why is he always fighting us and
trying to destroy all the Destiny Stones?

212
00:10:53,740 --> 00:10:55,560
This only he can answer.

213
00:10:55,840 --> 00:10:59,428
But how can we destroy Black
War Greymon if he's got a heart?

214
00:10:59,820 --> 00:11:02,291
It'd be like destroying you, Armadimon.

215
00:11:02,440 --> 00:11:04,480
What should we do? No, no.

216
00:11:04,720 --> 00:11:06,896
We have to destroy Black War Greymon.

217
00:11:07,900 --> 00:11:11,817
Even if he has a heart, it has been
turned evil by the powers of darkness.

218
00:11:11,900 --> 00:11:14,600
Will you let your anger rule you, TK?

219
00:11:31,160 --> 00:11:33,280
Be wary of the dark powers!

220
00:11:33,960 --> 00:11:35,920
See you guys! Be careful!

221
00:11:36,960 --> 00:11:39,372
Now let's go save us some Destiny Stones!

222
00:11:41,460 --> 00:11:42,640
Well, let's go.

223
00:11:42,980 --> 00:11:46,077
You know, TK, you can go
with the others if you want.

224
00:11:46,160 --> 00:11:47,278
It won't bother me.

225
00:11:47,900 --> 00:11:48,730
That's okay.

226
00:11:48,813 --> 00:11:51,580
Take care, Gabumon. You too. Thanks.

227
00:11:56,220 --> 00:11:57,760
You doing okay, Cody?

228
00:11:58,740 --> 00:11:59,700
I'm fine.

229
00:12:00,020 --> 00:12:02,844
I'll slow down a bit so
you can keep up with me.

230
00:12:04,380 --> 00:12:08,920
How can he be so angry and full of
vengeance one minute and so nice the next?

231
00:12:09,280 --> 00:12:10,692
I just don't understand.

232
00:12:12,520 --> 00:12:17,960
Would he really destroy Black War Greymon,
even though he knows he has a heart?

233
00:12:20,020 --> 00:12:22,480
There it is, the Destiny Stone.

234
00:12:23,880 --> 00:12:24,860
About time.

235
00:12:29,980 --> 00:12:32,040
And this time we got here first.

236
00:12:32,260 --> 00:12:33,848
Where is Black War Greymon?

237
00:12:33,960 --> 00:12:37,300
Getting closer, 50 meters,
40, he's inside the canyon.

238
00:12:44,700 --> 00:12:46,300
Here he comes!

239
00:12:46,720 --> 00:12:47,860
Let's do it!

240
00:12:48,000 --> 00:12:49,240
DNA Digiball!

241
00:12:53,400 --> 00:12:55,160
X-B-mon!

242
00:12:57,860 --> 00:12:58,900
Stingmon!

243
00:13:00,720 --> 00:13:02,600
DNA Digiball!

244
00:13:04,960 --> 00:13:07,000
I-Eel-Gramon!

245
00:13:09,280 --> 00:13:11,540
Digimon, digital monsters, Digimon!

246
00:13:15,980 --> 00:13:17,860
It's time to Digiball!

247
00:13:17,960 --> 00:13:18,840
DNA style!

248
00:13:23,960 --> 00:13:24,800
Aquilamon!

249
00:13:26,480 --> 00:13:27,320
Datamon!

250
00:13:29,980 --> 00:13:32,080
DNA Digiball too!

251
00:13:33,620 --> 00:13:35,937
Digimons, digital monsters, Digimon!

252
00:13:36,020 --> 00:13:37,140
Now let's jump in.

253
00:13:39,880 --> 00:13:40,710
SILFYMAR!

254
00:13:45,820 --> 00:13:46,879
DESPERATEL BUSTER!

255
00:13:52,480 --> 00:13:56,060
Your poor aim indicates you're
not a worthy opponent for me.

256
00:13:56,300 --> 00:13:57,660
Now step aside.

257
00:13:58,020 --> 00:13:59,257
You can try to get past me,

258
00:13:59,340 --> 00:14:03,046
